   "k": "wiofax",
   "en": "Peru-Bolivian Confederation"
  },
  {
   "k": "1g843mf",
   "en": "Peru began to rise from chaos of its civil wars in the early 20th century and made its self known on the geopolitical stage with a strong and stable regime throughout this time period. The infamous Great Depression passed through Peru and wreaked the countries economy and ushered in a new period of political instability."
  },
  {
   "k": "injyn6",
   "en": "Between 1932 and 1933, Peru entered a year long war with ⟦0⟧ over a territory dispute on their borders. The war resulted in a stalemate, and peace was soon brokered by the League of Nations, and the borders remained unchanged. Border skirmishes in the summer of 1941 led to all out war with ⟦1⟧ though the war eventually bogged down and became a stalemate. In the end Ecuador suffered more casualties and had to cede the disputed territory (this is represented in the game through a decision). As neither nation was supported by the major factions of the Allies or Axis it was the only war during World War Two not to actually be considered part of the then ongoing World War. During the war years Peru would be forced to trade more heavily with the ⟦2⟧ due to the loss of European trading partners. However in the early years of the pacific war due to the geographical position of Peru the United States would provide Lend Lease aid in the form of more modern American military equipment. This in turn would further increase tensions in the region as both Chile and Ecuador were concerned that Peru would make use of its newly modernized army to attempt to seize further territories it claimed.",
   "frags": 3
